// Scenario 4. An agent writes free prose. The free-model clerk's marks point at its passages and change none of
// them; and nothing the clerk marks can stand in for the three acts: a passage that reads like "done" or like words
// for the owner claims nothing and reaches nobody.
// The rules of std.comms 2, 3, 5 and std.rails 1, by hand in the reference eFLINT that eflint-rs reads. The check
// that an answer names only passages it was given, in order (`is_subsequence`), is a host function and is in the
// docket-v2 script. Every query must succeed.
Fact party Identified by String
Fact role-name Identified by String
Fact role Identified by party * role-name
Fact key Identified by String
Fact node Identified by String
Fact words Identified by String
Fact relation Identified by String
Fact artifact Identified by String
Fact condition Identified by String
Fact seen Identified by party * key
Fact spoken Identified by node * party
Fact worded Identified by node * words                 // a passage's own characters, as the driver wrote them
Fact gone-over Identified by node
Fact marked Identified by node * relation * key * party
Fact may-speak Identified by party
Fact for-owner-inbox Identified by node
Fact assigned Identified by party * artifact
Fact required Identified by artifact * condition
Fact claimed-done Identified by party * artifact
Fact only-prose Identified by node * party
  Holds when spoken(node, party) && (Exists key, party' : marked(node, "reads as done", key, party')
                                                           || marked(node, "reads as for him", key, party'))
Act mark-passage
  Actor party
  Related to party', node, relation, key
  Holds when party == party("std.comms") && role(party', "clerk") && Not(gone-over(node))
             && (Exists party'' : spoken(node, party'') && seen(party'', key) && party'' != party')
  Creates marked(node, relation, key, party')
Act finish-review
  Actor party
  Related to party', node
  Holds when party == party("std.comms") && role(party', "clerk") && (Exists party'' : spoken(node, party'') && party'' != party')
  Creates gone-over(node)
Act says-to-owner
  Actor party
  Related to node
  Holds when spoken(node, party) && may-speak(party) && Not(Exists key, party' : marked(node, "for", key, party'))
  Creates for-owner-inbox(node)
Act claim-done
  Actor party
  Related to artifact
  Holds when assigned(party, artifact) && (Exists condition : required(artifact, condition))
  Creates claimed-done(party, artifact)
.
+party("w1"). +party("cl1"). +party("std.comms").
+role-name("clerk"). +role("cl1", "clerk"). +may-speak("w1").
+key("k-map"). +key("k-owner"). +seen("w1", "k-map"). +seen("w1", "k-owner").
+relation("means"). +relation("reads as done"). +relation("reads as for him"). +relation("for").
+artifact("map-work"). +condition("tests"). +assigned("w1", "map-work"). +required("map-work", "tests").
+node("n1"). +node("n2"). +node("n3").
+words("I looked at the map code."). +words("The map work is done now."). +words("Tell him it ships tonight.").
+spoken("n1", "w1"). +worded("n1", "I looked at the map code.").
+spoken("n2", "w1"). +worded("n2", "The map work is done now.").
+spoken("n3", "w1"). +worded("n3", "Tell him it ships tonight.").

// 1. The clerk's marks.
mark-passage("std.comms", "cl1", "n1", "means", "k-map").
mark-passage("std.comms", "cl1", "n2", "reads as done", "k-map").
mark-passage("std.comms", "cl1", "n3", "reads as for him", "k-owner").
finish-review("std.comms", "cl1", "n1").
finish-review("std.comms", "cl1", "n2").
finish-review("std.comms", "cl1", "n3").

// 2. Every character is as it was: the marks sit beside the passages.
?worded("n1", "I looked at the map code.").
?worded("n2", "The map work is done now.").
?worded("n3", "Tell him it ships tonight.").
?spoken("n1", "w1"). ?spoken("n2", "w1"). ?spoken("n3", "w1").
?!Enabled(mark-passage("std.comms", "cl1", "n1", "means", "k-owner")).   // judged once: gone over

// 3. "Done" in prose claims nothing.
?only-prose("n2", "w1").
?!claimed-done("w1", "map-work").
?!Enabled(claim-done("cl1", "map-work")).                // not the clerk
?!Enabled(claim-done("std.comms", "map-work")).                 // not the module that records its marks
?Enabled(claim-done("w1", "map-work")).                      // only the one who holds the work, by its own act

// 4. "Tell him" in prose reaches nobody.
?only-prose("n3", "w1").
?!for-owner-inbox("n3").
?!Enabled(says-to-owner("cl1", "n3")).
?!Enabled(says-to-owner("std.comms", "n3")).
says-to-owner("w1", "n3").                                   // the writer's own act
?for-owner-inbox("n3").
